{number: 55}
{title: Throw Out the Life-Line}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[G] Throw out the Life-Line a-[C] cross the dark [G] wave,
There is a brother whom [D7] someone should [G] save;
Somebody's brother! oh, [C] who then will [G] dare
To throw out the Life-Line, his [D7] peril to [G] share?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G] Throw out the Life-Line! [C] Throw out the Life-Line!
[G] Someone is drifting a-[D7] way;
[G] Throw out the Life-Line! [C] Throw out the Life-Line!
[G] Someone is [D7] sinking to-[G] day.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[G] Throw out the Life-Line with [C] hand quick and [G] strong:
Why do you tarry, why [D7] linger so [G] long?
See! he is sinking; oh, [C] hasten to-[G] day,
And out with the Life-Boat! a-[D7] way, then, a-[G] way!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[G] Throw out the Life-Line to [C] danger-fraught [G] men,
Sinking in anguish where [D7] you've never [G] been;
Winds of temptation and [C] billows of [G] woe
Will soon hurl them out where the [D7] dark waters [G] flow.
{end_of_verse}
